  "conclusion": "NOT a B-button ceiling and NOT a velocity-capability ceiling. The model holds B on 91-97% of window frames (MORE than the expert's 77%) and reaches 2.60 px/frame during the approach, matching the expert's 2.5. The failure is WHERE it jumps: 56.2% of all A-onsets occur at x=585-600, i.e. already in contact with pipe 2, where median velocity is 0.00 px/frame. It runs to the pipe, stops, then jumps repeatedly from a standstill. SMB selects jump height from horizontal speed at takeoff, so a zero-velocity jump cannot clear a tall pipe no matter how long A is held. This is a timing/placement failure: the jump must start ~40-60px BEFORE the pipe, while still running.",
